# Scope — Plan 0001

> Teach junior Makina users three core Rust patterns — task state mutation, iteration, and aggregation — via a runnable todo list starter project.

## Why this plan

This starter plan introduces newcomers to the Makina task-driven workflow with three hands-on exercises. Each task teaches one pattern: toggling (state), counting (aggregation), and building on prior work (dependencies). By the end, a junior contributor has written production-grade Rust in a real plan, understood how Makina task sequences work, and shipped their first `cargo test / clippy / fmt` clean feature.

## In scope

- **0001 — Todo Core.** Three implementation tasks: `add-task-toggle` (mutation), `add-task-count` (aggregation), `print-open-summary` (composition).

## Out of scope

- Concurrency, persistence, or networking — this is a learning plan focused on single-threaded Rust fundamentals.
